WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.876
Repetition matters because skill improves through repeated attempts, feedback, and correction.

00:00:03.876 --> 00:00:06.965
A single explanation or demonstration rarely creates reliable performance.

00:00:06.965 --> 00:00:11.427
Repetition gives the learner multiple chances to notice the cue, make the decision,

00:00:11.427 --> 00:00:13.829
perform the step, and compare the result.

00:00:13.829 --> 00:00:17.948
It also helps parts of the skill become more fluent so attention

00:00:17.948 --> 00:00:19.664
can move to higher-level judgment.

00:00:19.664 --> 00:00:23.440
Exact repetition is useful early, but it is not always enough.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:25.843
If every practice attempt looks the same,

00:00:25.843 --> 00:00:29.962
the learner may memorize the surface pattern without understanding the underlying principle.

00:00:29.962 --> 00:00:32.364
Variation helps the skill become more flexible.

00:00:32.364 --> 00:00:35.453
Change the example, the context, the difficulty, the timing,

00:00:35.453 --> 00:00:39.572
or the constraints so the learner has to recognize what matters rather

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:41.288
than copy a fixed script.

00:00:41.288 --> 00:00:45.064
Practicing edge cases is especially useful when real work includes ambiguity.

00:00:45.064 --> 00:00:48.153
A strong troubleshooter needs more than the clean example.

00:00:48.153 --> 00:00:51.242
A strong communicator needs more than the friendly audience.

00:00:51.242 --> 00:00:54.331
A strong analyst needs more than the obvious signal.

00:00:54.331 --> 00:00:58.107
Variation teaches the learner how the skill behaves when conditions shift,

00:00:58.107 --> 00:01:01.539
evidence is incomplete, or the usual shortcut no longer works.

00:01:01.539 --> 00:01:02.912
Transfer is the goal.

00:01:02.912 --> 00:01:07.718
The learner should be able to apply the skill in a different task, context,

00:01:07.718 --> 00:01:08.747
or real-world situation.

00:01:08.747 --> 00:01:12.866
Retrieval and recall can support that transfer by asking learners to bring

00:01:12.866 --> 00:01:16.642
back the principle without the answer sitting in front of them.

00:01:16.642 --> 00:01:17.671
Repetition builds stability.

00:01:17.671 --> 00:01:18.701
Variation builds adaptability.

00:01:18.701 --> 00:01:22.820
Together they reduce brittle skill that only works in one familiar scenario.
